;; What clotran calls each name the upstream Clojure sources write. Read
;; only by upstream/derive (which writes src/clj/clojure and test/clj/clojure
;; from the copies here) and by scripts/oracle (which compares with clj,
;; whose answers name these classes). The runtime never sees it.
;;
;; :classes     a qualified name upstream writes -> clotran's class. A name
;;              not listed takes clotran.host.<snake_case simple name>.
;;              Written in Fortran: clotran.host, snake_case, a scalar its
;;              Fortran kind; written in Clojure: its deftype's own name.
;; :implicit    what every namespace imports: a name upstream writes bare,
;;              unimported (clj's (ns-imports 'user))
;; :constructors a class whose clotran type is built from its fields, not
;;              from the arguments upstream passes: its factory instead
;; :text        prose that names no one class, renamed as written (a plural)
;; :namespaces  upstream namespaces clotran provides under its own name
;; :words       what is left of the host's name in prose and in symbols
